.TH "PB-CONFIG-SYNC-APPLY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-sync-apply - Review the effective file configuration on this machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config sync apply [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Review the effective file configuration on this machine

.PP
Read and resolve the machine configuration, preview its effective assignment, then apply the confirmed revision. Use --confirm with the displayed code in noninteractive use. Synced files are plaintext in Git, and prior content remains in repository history.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	six-character confirmation code from the preview

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for apply

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print safe effective projection as JSON

.PP
\fB--repository\fP=""
	registered repository ID or name for initial bootstrap


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-sync(1)\fP
